L["READINESS_COLD_START"] = "Recommended: exit WoW normally and launch it again once to verify the span, workspace panels, and HUD recover correctly."
L["WIZARD_SKIP_HUD_CONFIRM_TEXT"] = "|cffffd100Finish without a Mainhand HUD layout?|r\n\nYour game view and workspace will stay configured, but action bars and unit frames may remain misplaced.\n\nTo complete setup now, click |cffffd100Back|r, then |cffffd100Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r while |cffffd100outside combat|r with |cffffd100Edit Mode closed|r.\n\n|cffffd100Finish Anyway|r saves setup without the HUD layout. Offhand will offer to resume after your next login or |cffffd100/reload|r; you can decline that reminder.\n\nYou can also finish later through |cffffd100Offhand settings > Recovery & Preview > Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r."
L["WIZARD_SKIP_HUD_COMPLETE"] = "Display setup saved. |cffffd100Mainhand HUD setup is still pending.|r Action bars and unit frames may remain misplaced."
L["ONBOARD_STEP_5_TITLE_NO_EDITMODE"] = "Classic interface preparation"
L["ONBOARD_STEP_5_BODY_NO_EDITMODE"] = "This client does not expose Blizzard's modern Edit Mode layout system, so no generated Mainhand HUD layout is required. The calibration wizard will finish after UI size is confirmed.\n\nAfter calibration, place ordinary movable windows such as the map, bags, and character panel on the Offhand workspace. Offhand will preserve their supported positions and visibility."
L["ONBOARD_STEP_6_BODY_NO_EDITMODE"] = "The installation checks are complete. Continue into the four-step calibration wizard to confirm monitor orientation, the physical seam, Mainhand aspect ratio and UI size. This client does not require a generated Blizzard Edit Mode layout, so finishing UI-size calibration completes setup.\n\nYou can reopen this guide later from /offhand guide or the Help tab."
L["STEP_4_HELP_NO_EDITMODE"] = "Choose a comfortable UI size. This client does not require a generated Blizzard Edit Mode layout, so Finish Setup completes calibration."
L["ONBOARD_STEP_5_BODY_EDITMODE"] = "This client manages action bars and other protected combat controls through Blizzard Edit Mode. The calibration wizard ends with Create Mainhand HUD Layout. Press it outside combat with Edit Mode closed; Offhand will create and select a Mainhand-safe copy, then ask you to reload.\n\nThe disabled button below is a visual preview. After setup, the same action remains available in Offhand Monitor > Recovery & Preview whenever the generated layout needs to be refreshed or rebuilt."
L["ONBOARD_STEP_6_BODY_EDITMODE"] = "The installation checks are complete. Continue into the calibration wizard to confirm monitor orientation, the physical seam, Mainhand aspect ratio and UI size. Because this client exposes Blizzard Edit Mode, the final step creates and selects the required Mainhand HUD layout; setup is fully ready after that succeeds.\n\nYou can reopen this guide later from /offhand guide or the Help tab."
L["STEP_4_HELP_EDITMODE"] = "Choose a comfortable UI size. Click Next to create the required Mainhand HUD layout as the final setup step on this client."
L["MSG_MANUAL_CANVAS_REMEMBERED"] = "%s memorizzato a %dx%d. Offhand riutilizzerà questa disposizione quando la dimensione della finestra corrisponde."
L["MSG_MANUAL_CANVAS_REMEMBER_FAILED"] = "Impossibile memorizzare la finestra corrente (%s)."
L["MSG_GEOMETRY_SOURCE_CHANGED"] = "Sorgente geometria cambiata in %s."
L["MSG_GEOMETRY_SOURCE_USAGE"] = "Uso: /offhand geometry auto, manual o exact."
L["CARD_MANUAL_CANVAS"] = "Finestra memorizzata"
L["BTN_REMEMBER_CURRENT_WINDOW"] = "Memorizza finestra corrente"
L["BTN_REMEMBER_CURRENT_WINDOW_TIP_TITLE"] = "Memorizza questa dimensione"
L["BTN_REMEMBER_CURRENT_WINDOW_TIP_DESC"] = "Conferma che la finestra WoW corrente è posizionata correttamente. Offhand riutilizzerà la disposizione dopo il riavvio quando la dimensione corrisponde."
L["MANUAL_CANVAS_DEFAULT_NAME"] = "Area memorizzata"
L["MANUAL_CANVAS_UNREMEMBERED"] = "Nessuna finestra indipendente è stata confermata. Posiziona WoW con FancyZones o manualmente, regola la divisione e memorizzala."
L["MANUAL_CANVAS_MATCHED"] = "%s è attivo (%s), misurato a %dx%d. La posizione nativa della finestra resta confermata visivamente da te."
L["MANUAL_CANVAS_MISMATCH"] = "La finestra corrente di %dx%d non corrisponde a un'area memorizzata. Offhand usa una geometria sicura a schermo singolo."
L["ONBOARD_USE_FANCYZONES"] = "Use FancyZones"
L["ONBOARD_METHOD_FANCYZONES_SELECTED"] = "FancyZones selected. Snap WoW into your saved zone, then continue."
L["POPUP_BTN_SETUP_GUIDE"] = "Window Setup"
L["POWERTOYS_LINK_TEXT"] = "Microsoft PowerToys includes FancyZones for saved window layouts. Install it from the Microsoft Store or another official source using the Microsoft guide below, enable FancyZones, then create one Canvas zone for the complete WoW window."
L["ONBOARD_STEP_2_BODY"] = "On Windows, we recommend the Microsoft Store Companion for exact monitor geometry and borderless placement.\n\nFancyZones remains an option for an existing PowerToys setup. Manual resizing works on any platform. Portable Companion builds are available for Linux/Wine.\n\nChoose the method you will use to place WoW, then continue calibration."
L["ONBOARD_STEP_3_BODY"] = "Use standard Windowed mode. Place WoW with a saved FancyZones Canvas zone, Companion Span WoW Now, or manual resizing across the intended displays or ultrawide region."
L["ONBOARD_STEP_4_BODY"] = "Place WoW using the selected method. FancyZones and manual placement require one explicit canvas confirmation. Companion users should span and Reload UI for exact topology."
L["ONBOARD_STATUS_CHECK_PROMPT"] = "Place WoW with FancyZones, Companion, or manually, then click Next."
L["ONBOARD_STATUS_METHOD_REQUIRED"] = "Choose FancyZones, Companion, or manual setup before continuing."
L["ONBOARD_STATUS_MANUAL_CONFIRM"] = "This independent window needs confirmation because WoW cannot report its physical display boundaries or native position."
L["ONBOARD_MANUAL_CONFIRM_TEXT"] = "|cffffd100Confirm this Offhand window|r\n\nContinue only if FancyZones or you deliberately positioned WoW across the intended displays or ultrawide region. Offhand will remember this canvas size."
L["ONBOARD_MANUAL_CONFIRM_TEXT_FOREVER"] = "|cffffd100Confirm this Forever window|r\n\nForever cannot report the native window position. Continue only if FancyZones or you deliberately positioned WoW across the intended displays or ultrawide region."
L["ONBOARD_MANUAL_CONFIRM_ACCEPT"] = "Remember Window"
L["HELP_OVERVIEW_BODY"] = "Use Window Setup to choose FancyZones, Companion, or manual placement. Then run calibration and prepare the Mainhand HUD layout where supported."
L["HELP_SETUP_BODY"] = "1. Use standard Windowed mode.\n2. Choose FancyZones on Windows, Companion for Linux/Wine or exact topology, or manual placement.\n3. Position and remember the window.\n4. Complete calibration.\n5. Fully exit and relaunch once to verify it."
L["HELP_COMPANION_TITLE"] = "Window placement: FancyZones, Companion, or manual"
L["HELP_COMPANION_BODY"] = "WoW addons cannot resize the native game window. FancyZones can restore a saved Windows zone; Companion remains useful for Linux/Wine and exact topology; manual placement is also supported. Offhand validates the resulting canvas, not the external tool."
L["HELP_COLD_LAUNCH_BODY"] = "Reapply the saved FancyZones zone, Companion span, or manual size when WoW starts, then let Offhand validate the remembered canvas. Companion may be closed after spanning unless your platform or recovery workflow requires it."
L["HELP_WELCOME_BODY"] = "The first-launch guide covers FancyZones, Companion, and manual placement before calibration. Reopen it with /offhand guide."
L["MSG_SPAN_GUIDE"] = "Position Windowed WoW with FancyZones, Companion, or manual resizing, then confirm the canvas in Offhand."
L["POPUP_WELCOME_WARNING_TEXT"] = "|cffffd100Welcome to Offhand!|r\n\nSet WoW to standard Windowed mode, then choose FancyZones, Offhand Companion, or manual resizing. Offhand validates the resulting canvas and guides calibration."
L["WIZARD_WELCOME_TEXT"] = "|cffffd100Welcome to Offhand!|r This wizard verifies the current WoW canvas. Exact Companion topology is used when available; FancyZones and manual windows use the canvas remembered during window setup."
L["READINESS_RECOVERY_FOREVER"] = "SavedVariables persistence; Companion bridge optional"
L["POPUP_CONFIRM_EXISTING_WINDOW_TEXT"] = "|cffffd100Confirm your existing Offhand window|r\n\nThis update validates independently positioned windows before applying a split. Your saved profile has not been removed. If WoW is positioned correctly, choose Remember Current Window. Otherwise choose Not Now and run /offhand guide after positioning it."
L["MAINHAND_GAMEPAD_PRESET_APPLIED"] = "Applied the Mainhand translation to the active Gamepad preset and moved %d HUD systems."
L["MAINHAND_GAMEPAD_PRESET_RELOAD_TEXT"] = "Offhand updated the active Gamepad preset for Mainhand. Type /reload now to verify that Offhand restores the translated preset after loading."
L["CARD_USER_MEDIA"] = "4. Background Studio"
L["USER_MEDIA_ENABLE"] = "Use installed custom background"
L["USER_MEDIA_ENABLE_TIP_TITLE"] = "Custom Canvas Background"
L["USER_MEDIA_ENABLE_TIP_DESC"] = "Uses the optional Offhand User Media package generated by the Background Studio. Offhand safely returns to its normal theme when the package is unavailable or invalid."
L["USER_MEDIA_STATUS_AVAILABLE"] = "Ready: %dx%d image in a %dx%d texture (schema %d)."
L["USER_MEDIA_STATUS_MISSING"] = "No usable Offhand User Media package was found. Generate one on the Offhand website, install it beside Offhand, then fully restart WoW."
L["USER_MEDIA_STATUS_DISABLED"] = "Offhand User Media is installed but disabled in the AddOns list. Enable it, then fully restart WoW."
L["USER_MEDIA_STATUS_INVALID"] = "The installed Offhand User Media metadata is invalid or unsupported. Generate a fresh package in Background Studio."
L["USER_MEDIA_STATUS_LEGACY"] = "This media package uses the older Lua format. Open it with Background Studio's Update package option and generate a new code-free replacement."
L["USER_MEDIA_FIT_PACKAGE"] = "Studio recommendation"
L["USER_MEDIA_FIT_FILL"] = "Fill"
L["USER_MEDIA_FIT_FIT"] = "Fit"
L["USER_MEDIA_FIT_STRETCH"] = "Stretch"
L["USER_MEDIA_FIT_TIP_TITLE"] = "Background Fit"
L["USER_MEDIA_FIT_TIP_DESC"] = "Use the Studio recommendation or override how the installed image fills the Offhand canvas. Crop focus, zoom, opacity, darkening, and matte color remain defined by the generated package."
L["USER_MEDIA_RESTART_NOTE"] = "Replacing the media package requires a full WoW restart so the client can reload the texture."

L["HUD_SETUP_REMINDER_TEXT"] = "|cffffd100Your display setup is saved. HUD setup is still pending.|r\n\nAction bars and unit frames may still span both screens.\n\nClick |cffffd100Resume HUD setup|r to open the final calibration step. While |cffffd100outside combat|r with |cffffd100Blizzard Edit Mode closed|r, click |cffffd100Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r and follow the prompts.\n\n|cffffd100Don't remind me|r stops automatic reminders. You can always finish later through |cffffd100Offhand settings > Recovery & Preview > Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r."

L["HUD_SETUP_RESUME"] = "Resume HUD setup"

L["HUD_SETUP_DECLINE"] = "Don't remind me"

L["HUD_SETUP_CALIBRATE"] = "Calibration"

L["IDENTIFY_UNSPANNED_COMPANION"] = "Companion placement has not been confirmed for this window.\n\n1. Click |cffffd100Back to setup|r.\n2. In Companion, select your screens and Mainhand, then click |cffffd100Span WoW Now|r.\n3. Return to WoW, click |cffffd100Reload UI|r, then |cffffd100Confirm placement|r.\n\nFor physical monitor numbers, use |cffffd100Windows Settings > System > Display > Identify|r."

L["IDENTIFY_BACK_TO_SETUP"] = "Back to setup"

L["WIZARD_SKIP_HUD_NEXT"] = "To finish, open |cffffd100Offhand settings > Recovery & Preview > Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r while outside combat with Edit Mode closed. Offhand will offer to resume after your next login or |cffffd100/reload|r; you can decline that reminder."

-- Setup recovery actions (English fallback until translated).
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_SPAN_TITLE"] = "Load your window placement before calibration"
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_INTRO"] = "Setup is paused. Follow the steps below, then continue from this calibration step."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_SPAN_BODY"] = "Offhand has not confirmed the game window's placement. Windowed mode alone does not complete this step.\n\n|cffffd100Using Companion?|r\n1. In Companion, select your screens and Mainhand, then click |cffffd100Span WoW Now|r while logged into the game world.\n2. Return here and click |cffffd100Reload UI|r below to load the display geometry. This wizard will resume at the same step.\n\n|cffffd100Using FancyZones or manual placement?|r\nClick |cffffd100Return to window setup|r, place WoW across the intended screens, then confirm the placement in the guide.\n\nMaximizing normally fills one monitor; it does not replace spanning."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_WINDOW_SETUP"] = "Return to window setup"
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_MAX_TITLE"] = "Make room in Blizzard Edit Mode"
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_MAX_BODY"] = "Blizzard's custom layout list is full. Offhand needs space to create your Mainhand HUD layout. Your display calibration is still saved.\n\n1. Click |cffffd100Open Blizzard Edit Mode|r below. You can also reach it through |cffffd100Escape > Edit Mode|r.\n2. Open the |cffffd100layout dropdown|r at the top of Edit Mode. Choose an unused custom layout, then its |cffffd100Delete|r option and confirm. Export it first if you may want it later. Delete only a layout you no longer need.\n3. Close Edit Mode. Offhand returns to this step automatically. Click |cffffd100Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r again.\n\nOffhand will not delete a layout for you."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_OPEN_EDITMODE"] = "Open Blizzard Edit Mode"
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_RETRY"] = "Back to HUD setup"
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_EDITMODE_COMBAT"] = "Leave combat before opening Blizzard Edit Mode. Then click Open Blizzard Edit Mode again."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_EDITMODE_MANUAL"] = "Edit Mode could not be opened here. Press Escape, choose Edit Mode, then use its layout dropdown. Return with /offhand wizard if needed."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_RETURNED"] = "Back in HUD setup. Click Create Mainhand HUD Layout to try again. No layout was deleted by Offhand."
L["MAINHAND_LAYOUT_SPAN_ACTIONS"] = "Window placement is not confirmed. In Companion, click |cffffd100Span WoW Now|r, return to WoW and |cffffd100Reload UI|r. For FancyZones or manual placement, open |cffffd100/offhand guide|r to confirm the window before calibration."
L["ONBOARD_SPAN_NOT_MAXIMIZE"] = "Maximizing normally fills one screen. Use |cffffd100Span WoW Now|r to place WoW across the selected screens, then |cffffd100Reload UI|r here."

-- Action-led recovery and calibration progress (English fallback until translated).
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_COMPANION_BODY"] = "Companion setup is selected, but Offhand has not confirmed its display geometry.\n\n1. In Companion, select your screens and Mainhand. While logged into the game world, click |cffffd100Span WoW Now|r.\n2. Return here and click |cffffd100Reload UI|r below. Calibration will resume at this step.\n\nMaximizing normally fills one screen; it does not replace spanning. If you intended to use another method, choose |cffffd100Return to window setup|r."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_FANCYZONES_BODY"] = "FancyZones placement is not confirmed. Reloading alone will not position the window.\n\n1. Choose |cffffd100Return to window setup|r below.\n2. Use |cffffd100Windowed|r mode and snap WoW into your combined Canvas zone.\n3. Visually check both screens, click |cffffd100Confirm placement|r, then |cffffd100Remember Window|r when prompted.\n\nReturn to calibration after confirming the window. Your saved calibration values are retained."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_MANUAL_BODY"] = "Manual placement is not confirmed. Reloading alone will not position the window.\n\n1. Choose |cffffd100Return to window setup|r below.\n2. Use |cffffd100Windowed|r mode, then drag and resize WoW across the intended screens or ultrawide region.\n3. Visually check the placement, click |cffffd100Confirm placement|r, then |cffffd100Remember Window|r when prompted.\n\nThis is your confirmation; Offhand cannot detect physical monitor boundaries for manual placement."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_CHOOSE_BODY"] = "Choose how to place WoW before calibrating it.\n\nClick |cffffd100Choose placement method|r below. The guide will walk you through Companion, FancyZones or manual placement, then return to calibration. Your saved calibration values are retained."
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_CHOOSE_METHOD"] = "Choose placement method"
L["WIZARD_RECOVERY_RECHECK"] = "Check placement again"
L["WIZARD_RESTART"] = "Restart calibration"
L["WIZARD_RESTART_NOTICE"] = "Calibration restarted at step 1. Existing values and HUD layouts have not been reset."
L["WIZARD_RESUMED"] = "Continuing calibration at step %d of %d. Saved values are retained; use Restart calibration to review from step 1."
L["HUD_FAILURE_COMBAT"] = "Leave combat, then click |cffffd100Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r again. No HUD layout was created by this attempt."
L["HUD_FAILURE_EDITMODE_OPEN"] = "Close |cffffd100Blizzard Edit Mode|r first, then click |cffffd100Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r again outside combat. Save any personal Edit Mode changes before closing it."
L["HUD_FAILURE_DISABLED"] = "Offhand is disabled. Open |cffffd100/offhand|r, enable Offhand, then return to |cffffd100/offhand wizard|r to continue calibration."
L["HUD_FAILURE_API"] = "This client does not expose the Blizzard Edit Mode tools needed to create the HUD layout. Check that you installed Offhand for the correct WoW client. You can arrange protected HUD elements with your client's own controls. For help, collect |cffffd100/offhand diag|r and your client/build for support."
L["HUD_FAILURE_UNAVAILABLE"] = "Blizzard's Edit Mode layouts are not available yet. Close Edit Mode, |cffffd100/reload|r once, then reopen |cffffd100/offhand wizard|r. If this repeats, collect |cffffd100/offhand diag|r for support. Do not delete layouts to solve this message."
L["HUD_FAILURE_STATE"] = "Offhand could not access this character's saved setup state. |cffffd100/reload|r once and reopen |cffffd100/offhand wizard|r. If it repeats, fully exit WoW and contact support with |cffffd100/offhand diag|r. Do not delete your saved settings."
L["HUD_FAILURE_SOURCE"] = "Select a source HUD layout in |cffffd100Escape > Edit Mode|r, then close Edit Mode and retry |cffffd100Create Mainhand HUD Layout|r. Choose the layout whose controls you want to keep on Mainhand."
L["HUD_FAILURE_REPAIR"] = "Offhand could not safely rebuild the selected protected HUD frame. Outside combat, use |cffffd100Blizzard Edit Mode|r or the owning addon's controls to position it on Mainhand. If needed, send |cffffd100/offhand diag|r and a screenshot to support."
L["HUD_FAILURE_ALREADY"] = "No default HUD anchors needed moving in the selected layout. Check that its controls are on Mainhand in |cffffd100Blizzard Edit Mode|r. If setup still cannot finish, collect |cffffd100/offhand diag|r for support instead of deleting or resetting the layout."
L["HUD_FAILURE_SAVE"] = "Blizzard did not accept saving the Mainhand HUD layout. Close Edit Mode, leave combat and retry once. If it repeats, collect |cffffd100/offhand diag|r for support. This message does not mean the layout list is full; do not delete layouts unless Offhand explicitly reports that limit."
L["HUD_FAILURE_ACTIVATE"] = "Offhand prepared a Mainhand HUD layout but could not select it automatically. Open |cffffd100Escape > Edit Mode|r, select the generated Offhand Mainhand layout, save and close Edit Mode, then return to calibration. If selection fails, collect |cffffd100/offhand diag|r for support."
L["HUD_FAILURE_CONTROLLER"] = "Your controller UI owns this protected HUD layout. Use its own layout controls to position action bars and unit frames on Mainhand. Offhand can still manage supported ordinary panels. For help with this client/controller combination, collect |cffffd100/offhand diag|r for support."
L["HUD_FAILURE_UNKNOWN"] = "The HUD layout could not be completed. Close Edit Mode and leave combat, then retry once. If it repeats, send |cffffd100/offhand diag|r, your versions and the steps you followed to support. Do not reset or delete layouts without a specific reason."
-- Extra Abilities recovery (English fallback until translated).
L["RECOVERY_EXTRA_ABILITIES"] = "Recover Extra Abilities"
L["RECOVERY_EXTRA_ABILITIES_LABEL"] = "Return quest and zone ability buttons to Mainhand."
L["RECOVERY_EXTRA_ABILITIES_DESC"] = "Resets Extra Abilities to a visible Mainhand position in the Offhand HUD layout, including custom anchors. Preserves other systems in an existing Offhand layout. Use outside combat with Edit Mode closed, then reload. A button appears only when the game provides an ability."

-- Missing-only recovery and confirmation messages (English fallback).
L["RECOVERY_MISSING"] = "Recover Missing UI"
L["RECOVERY_MISSING_LABEL"] = "Recover missing supported UI. Visible elements stay in place."
L["RECOVERY_MISSING_CONFIRM"] = "Recover missing UI?\n\nOnly fully off-screen supported windows and HUD elements will be moved. Anything visible on either display stays where it is.\n\nInactive abilities and interaction windows will stay closed.\n\nRecovered elements may overlap and need adjustment. HUD repairs can change the native layout and may require a reload.\n\nContinue?"
L["RECOVERY_MISSING_RESULT"] = "Recovery: %d windows moved, %d HUD systems repaired, %d skipped or unavailable."
L["RECOVERY_GATHER_CONFIRM"] = "Move all supported visible Offhand windows to Mainhand? This changes their current positions and saved placements, including windows that are already reachable. Protected HUD systems remain under Blizzard Edit Mode. Unintended layout changes or overlapping windows may result. Continue?"
L["RECOVERY_LAYOUT_CONFIRM"] = "Create or rebuild the Mainhand HUD layout? This can reposition HUD systems that are already visible and replace edits in the generated Offhand layout. Unintended layout changes may result. Use Recover Missing UI to preserve visible elements. Continue?"
L["RECOVERY_EXTRA_CONFIRM"] = "Reset Extra Abilities to Mainhand? This changes its anchor even if the ability button is already visible. Other systems in the existing Offhand HUD layout are preserved, but native layout application may cause unintended layout changes. Continue?"

-- Native workspace Escape support (English fallback until translated).
L["CHECK_ESC_PERSIST_LIMITED_DESC"] = "Keeps supported Offhand windows open on Escape while out of combat. Close buttons and interaction endings still work normally. Protected UI modes retain native behavior."
